# Paired validator: prospective development diagnostic

Idea coreset-adaptive-comparison-v1, revision1, goal contract1. This plan is written after native_pilot_v1, before validator outcomes. It consumes the accepted source/math audit in the parent project. This is an implementation of known concentration and adaptive-selection ideas, not an originality claim.

Hypothesis: a valid pairwise adaptive selector over frozen sample-median candidates can reduce validation work relative to a fixed final look while adding little cost compared with exact coordinate median. This does not imply that it is faster than a single uniform sample or that pairwise certification proves globally near-optimal coreset quality.
Native data: the already exposed first100000 cleaned Taxi rows, with first10000 as smaller cost diagnostic. Development only. Seeds 101..112, three fixed nested iid-with-replacement training samples of sizes32,128,512, independent validation RNG. These12 seeds are a feasibility/variance pilot, not a nominal5% error-rate verification.
K=3 fixed candidates; P=3 distinct pairs; geometric validation looks m=64,128,256,512,1024,2048,4096,8192. δ=.05 is split over the3 pairs and8 deterministic looks. For D_ij=||c_i-c_j||_1, Z_ij(x)=||x-c_i||_1-||x-c_j||_1 is in[-D_ij,D_ij]. Simultaneous Hoeffding radius r_ij(m)=D_ij*sqrt(2*log(2*P*8/δ)/m). Exact D=0 is equality. Compute per-coordinate differences to reduce cancellation; substantive range violations invalidate the run.
Set ε=.01 and rho=ε/(2+ε). A candidate i is certified against the finite pool if all pairwise upper bounds Δ_ij+r_ij<=rho*D_ij. Triangle inequality establishes F_i<=(1+ε)F_j for all j on the coverage event. This proves only finite-pool relative quality. If no candidate is certified by8192 samples, use exact coordinate median and count the full failed validation cost.
Arms: adaptive geometric-look policy; same pool and independent validation sequence with only final look8192; exact coordinate median; fixed uniform sample medians at32/128/512. Alternate adaptive/fixed order by seed. Each selection path includes its own candidate construction, RNG, validation, confidence computations and fallback. Offline full-data scoring is outside algorithm time for every arm.
Outputs: all seeds and arms, pathwall/CPU, train draws512 and validation draws, fallback, finite-pool certificate actual ratio, relative excess full-data cost, comparisons with exact and fixed uniform. Save selected centers. Never use offline optimum during selection unless declared fallback. Shared-host timings are descriptive; no broad speedup claim. Singlethread, one numerical process,4GiB AS,120s timeout.
Decision: any false mathematical certificate beyond floating tolerance -> inspect math/implementation; predominantly cap/fallback or adverse whole-path cost -> reject practical efficiency of this conservative policy on these native development cases and investigate the limiting bound/target. Success -> stronger existing methods and fresh conditions still required. Near-ties and easy exact solvers are legitimate failure regimes. Retain all results.
